{{!
    @template theme_nit/navbar_gear_nav

    Core's navigation rows inside the gear dropdown, under their own
    "Navigation" heading: My courses, Site administration (Home and Dashboard
    are deliberately left out). Built by
    theme_nit\output\core_renderer::navbar_gear_nav() from $PAGE->primarynav
    rather than from the template's `mobileprimarynav`, so the custom menu items
    (which core merges into that list) stay where the administrator put them —
    as titles on the bar.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * items - [{text, url, isactive, haschildren, children:[{text, url, isactive}]}]

    Example context (json):
    {
        "items": [
            {"text": "My courses", "url": "https://example.com/my/courses.php", "isactive": true},
            {"text": "Site administration", "url": "https://example.com/admin/search.php", "isactive": false}
        ]
    }
}}
<h6 class="dropdown-header">{{#str}}navigation, core{{/str}}</h6>
{{#items}}
    <a class="dropdown-item{{#isactive}} active{{/isactive}}" href="{{{url}}}" {{#isactive}}aria-current="true"{{/isactive}}>{{{text}}}</a>
    {{#haschildren}}
        {{#children}}
            <a class="dropdown-item nit-navmenu-child{{#isactive}} active{{/isactive}}" href="{{{url}}}" {{#isactive}}aria-current="true"{{/isactive}}>{{{text}}}</a>
        {{/children}}
    {{/haschildren}}
{{/items}}
